A rotary electric machine includes a rotor and a stator. The stator has:

- a stator core provided with slots or teeth;
- coils mounted on or inserted into the stator core;
- a first insulating-paper portion arranged between the stator core and the coils;
- a second insulating-paper portion adjoining or overlapping the first insulating-paper portion; and
- an insulating resin disposed between the first and second insulating-paper portions.

The resin bonds and seals the paper portions, preventing gaps, displacement, and electrical leakage at their joint. This construction improves insulation reliability between the coils and the stator core while allowing a compact stator structure and facilitating assembly.
